# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout and
# warns on every single `git add` -- 50+ warnings per commit for this project. That is
# noise that trains you to ignore warnings, which is exactly how the real ones get
# missed. It also means a file edited on Windows and the same file edited on Linux
# would show as different blobs, producing phantom diffs.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs binary. The explicit rules below pin the files
# where guessing goes wrong.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.js   text eol=lf
*.jsx  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Never touched: lockfiles and images must keep their exact bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff2 binary
